The '''Bugatti Centodieci''' ([[Italian language|Italian]] for "110")<ref name="bloom"/> is a limited production [[Mid-engine design|mid-engine]] [[sports car]] produced by French automotive manufacturer [[Bugatti Automobiles|Bugatti]]. The car is a [[Homage (arts)|homage]] to the [[Bugatti EB 110]] and a celebration of the [[Bugatti]] marque's 110th birthday. It was revealed on 16{{nbsp}}August 2019 at "The Quail – A Motorsports Gathering" in California, United States.<ref>{{cite press release |title=Bugatti Centodieci – Exclusive Small Series in Extraordinary Design |url=https://newsroom.bugatti.com/press-releases/bugatti-centodieci-exclusive-small-series-in-extraordinary-design |access-date=23 December 2022 |publisher=Bugatti |date=16 August 2019 |location=Molsheim}}</ref> The Centodieci is 20&nbsp;kg lighter than the [[Bugatti Chiron]], and has an {{cvt|8.0|L|cuin|1|abbr=on}} quad-turbocharged W16 engine, rated at {{cvt|1600|PS|kW PS hp|0|order=out}} at 7,000&nbsp;rpm. Production of the Centodieci was limited to 10{{nbsp}}units priced at {{euro|8 million}} (approximately $10{{nbsp}}million at the 2019 exchange rate) each.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Barlow |first1=Jason |title=This is the £9m Bugatti Centodieci |url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/supercars/ps9m-bugatti-centodieci |accessdate=17 August 2019 |work=Top Gear |date=16 August 2019 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Batchelor |first1=James |title=New Bugatti Centodieci revives spirit of iconic EB110 |url=https://www.autoexpress.co.uk/bugatti/107665/new-bugatti-centodieci-revives-spirit-of-iconic-eb110 |accessdate=18 August 2019 |work=Auto Express |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.esquire.com/lifestyle/cars/a28720427/new-bugatti-retro-centodieci/|title=The New $8.8 Million Bugatti Centodieci Is a Retro '90s Hypercar Dream|last=Sintumuang|first=Kevin|date=2019-08-16|website=Esquire|language=en-US|access-date=2019-08-19}}</ref>

== Design ==
Based on the [[Bugatti Chiron|Chiron]], the car takes design cues from the [[Bugatti EB 110|EB 110]] such as the five round air intakes which resemble a diamond and the wedge shaped design language. A small horse shoe radiator grille present below the headlamps further harks back to the EB 110. Narrow headlights with LED daytime running function and sharp grooves are used to create an aggressive appearance. The rear consists of eight tail lights along with matt-black quad exhaust pipes placed on either side of a large diffuser, complete with an underbody spoiler and a fixed overhanging rear wing. Due to the use of computer assisted 3D design techniques and the use of Virtual Reality technology, the design team was able to complete the design of the Centodieci in six months.<ref name="engadget"/><ref name="www.bugatti.com">{{cite web |title=Bugatti Centodieci |url=https://www.bugatti.com/one-off/centodieci/ |website=www.bugatti.com |accessdate=18 August 2019 |language=en |archive-date=18 August 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190818144455/https://www.bugatti.com/one-off/centodieci/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.designboom.com/technology/bugatti-centodieci-eb110-the-quail-08-21-2019/|title=a blast from the past: $9 million bugatti centodieci hyper sports car|date=18 August 2019|first=Tim |last=Spears|publisher=Designboom|access-date=28 August 2019}}</ref> Compared to the Chiron, the Centodieci is fitted with an additional air intake near the oil cooler and an engine bay cover manufactured from glass.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Bugatti's EB110-inspired Centodieci is one step closer to production|url=https://www.autoblog.com/2021/10/14/bugatti-centodieci-testing-hot-weather/|access-date=2021-10-14|website=Autoblog|language=en}}</ref>

