== Performance ==
The Centodieci is capable of accelerating from 0-{{convert|100|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}} in 2.4 seconds, 0-{{convert|200|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}} in 6.1 seconds and 0-{{convert|300|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}} in 13.1 seconds with a top speed electronically limited to {{convert|380|km/h|mph|abbr=on}} ({{convert|482|km/h|mph|abbr=on}} with the top speed key) and has a curb weight of {{convert|4356|lb|kg|abbr=on|order=flip}}.<ref name="www.bugatti.com" />

== Production ==
10 units of the Centodieci were produced for customers, in addition to pre-production and test cars. The Centodieci were hand-built in Bugatti's [[Molsheim]] factory and deliveries to customers started in June 2022.<ref name="bloom">{{Cite news|title=Bugatti Channels Early '90s Supercar Swag in New $8.9 Million Auto|url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2019-08-16/bugatti-centodieci-revives-spirit-of-eb110-photos-specs-price|last=Elliot|first=Hannah|date=August 16, 2019|work=Bloomberg|access-date=August 20, 2019|language=en}}</ref> On 19 December 2022, the tenth and last Bugatti Centodieci was delivered.<ref>{{cite press release |title=Bugatti delivers the tenth – and final – centodieci hyper sports car |url=https://www.bugatti.com/media/news/2022/bugatti-delivers-the-tenth-and-final-centodieci-hyper-sports-car/ |access-date=23 December 2022 |publisher=Bugatti |date=19 December 2022 |location=Molsheim}}</ref> 

